.th P I MAR/76
.sh NAME
p \*- flexible pagination of output
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd p
[ \fB-m\fR ]
[ \fB+m\fR ]
[ \fB-s\fR ]
"pattern"
.bd -r
.bd -t
.bd -c
file ...
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it P
reads from its input, breaking on 18 line pages and removing
underlined words and form feeds. If no files are given then the standard
input is read; if more than one file is given then the filename is given
before the file is printed. Between pages it reads a carriage return
from the terminal in no echo. If delete is hit while printing
a file, then
.it p
prints the last filename, and the page/line# last read. The meanings
of the various options are: 
.ft I
.lp +8 7
option	meaning
.ft R
.s3
.lp +8 7
\fB-n\fR	Set pagesize to n. Default is 18.
.s3
.lp +8 7
\fB+m\fR[l]	Skip \fBm\fR pages. If 'l' is given, \fBm\fR lines.
.s3
.lp +8 7
\fB-r\fR	Don't escape frog's, formfeeds and underlines.
.s3
.lp +8 7
\fB-c\fR	Continuous form.
.s3
.lp +8 7
\fB-s\fR	Skip until pattern GLOB(VIII) is matched.
.i0
.dt
.sh BUGS
